\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
We develop a unified, non-perturbative mathematical framework for quantum gravity and gauge field theories formulated on the simplicial product manifold $\mathcal{M} = \Delta_4 \times \Delta_2$, where $\Delta_4$ is the standard 4-simplex defining the spacetime triangulation and $\Delta_2$ is the internal flavor 2-simplex. The framework replaces the uncritical extrapolation of smooth continuum manifolds and quadratic Hilbert--Einstein actions with an $L^\infty$-minimax variational principle coupled to non-local fractional integro-differential operators (Simplicial Beta-Laplacians).

Within this unified setting, we establish:
(1) An exact analytical derivation of the running spectral dimension from $d_s = 2$ in the trans-Planckian ultraviolet regime ($k \gg M_P$) down to $d_s = 4$ in the macroscopic infrared regime ($k \ll M_P$), ensuring power-counting ultraviolet renormalizability through Lifshitz-type scaling without Ostrogradsky ghost instabilities.
(2) In the Arnowitt--Deser--Misner (ADM) $3+1$ Hamiltonian formalism, spacelike Cauchy hypersurfaces minimizing the extrinsic curvature operator norm $\|\II\|_{L^\infty} \le \ell_P^{-1}$ uniformly bound the gravitational shear scalar $\sigma_{ij}\sigma^{ij} \le 3(\kappa^*)^2 - \frac{1}{3}K^2$, while the Planck pressure saturation barrier $P_{\mathrm{top}} \approx 4.63 \times 10^{113}\text{ Pa}$ replaces initial curvature singularities with a non-singular $C^{1,1}$ cosmological bounce, reproducing the effective bounce dynamics of Loop Quantum Cosmology.
(3) The wave-packet reduction process is modeled as a classical unilateral obstacle problem in Sobolev spaces governed by Luis Caffarelli's optimal $C^{1,1}$ free-boundary regularity, with transition probabilities corresponding to Liouville symplectic volume ratios on the Fubini--Study phase space of $\mathbb{C}P^N$.
(4) Fermionic fields formulated as inhomogeneous Dirac--K\"ahler differential forms on the simplicial complex circumvent the lattice Nielsen--Ninomiya doubling theorem, while the $S_3$ permutation symmetry of the internal flavor 2-simplex $\Delta_2$ dictates the replication of exactly $N_g = \dim(\Delta_2) + 1 \equiv 3$ chiral families.
(5) On the fundamental Gribov modular domain $\Omega \subset \mathcal{A}/\mathcal{G}$, chromomagnetic fluctuations are stabilized against the Savvidy instability, yielding a strictly positive Bakry--\'Emery Ricci bound $\mathrm{Ric}_\infty \ge K_{\mathrm{QCD}} > 0$, an energy gap $\Delta \ge \sqrt{K_{\mathrm{QCD}}} > 0$ for color-singlet excitations, and the Wilson area law via a positive Federer reach $\reach(\Omega) \ge 1/\kappa^*$.
(6) The parameter space of the Standard Model is geometrically constrained into the Planck dimensional triad $(\hbar, c, \ell_P)$, yielding the Koide lepton quotient $Q_l = 2/3$ from circulant $\mathbb{Z}_3$ orbits on $\Delta_2$, the Cabibbo angle $\sin\theta_C \approx 0.2261$, and an exact topological cancellation of quartic vacuum energy divergences $(1 - 1)^4 M_P^4 \equiv 0$ through alternating boundary orientations on $\partial \Delta_4$.

The mathematical identities, algebraic structures, and variational inequalities underlying the framework have been formally verified in the Lean~4 interactive theorem prover with zero unproven shortcuts (\texttt{0 sorry}).
\end{abstract}

