\section{Topological BCJ Double Copy and Emergent Spacetime}
\label{sec:bcj_double_copy}
% =========================================================================

The Bern--Carrasco--Johansson (BCJ) duality \cite{bern2008new} establishes that perturbative gravity scattering amplitudes factorize as the product of two gauge-theory amplitudes: $\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{gravity}} \sim \mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{YM}} \otimes \widetilde{\mathcal{A}}_{\mathrm{YM}}$.

On the simplicial lattice $\Delta_4$, this duality is realized geometrically:
\begin{equation}
    \label{eq:double_copy_exact}
    h_{\mu\nu}^{\mathrm{TT}}(\mathbf{x}) = \Tr\left( A_\mu(\mathbf{x}) \star_\Delta A_\nu(\mathbf{x}) \right),
\end{equation}
where $A_\mu$ is the Dirac--K\"ahler gauge 1-form on edges, and $h_{\mu\nu}^{\mathrm{TT}}$ is the physical graviton field on 2-faces.

Under continuous Graphon Ricci Flow on random simplicial connectivity kernels $W \in L^\infty([0, 1]^2)$:
\begin{equation}
    \partial_t W(t, x, y) = -2 \kappa_W(t, x, y) W(t, x, y),
\end{equation}
one-dimensional polymer bottlenecks with negative Ollivier Ricci curvature $\kappa_W \le -c/\epsilon < 0$ undergo topological neckpinch surgery, excising non-manifold branches in finite time $T_{\mathrm{surgery}} = \frac{\epsilon}{2c} \ln(1/\epsilon)$ and condensing Planckian foam into a smooth 4-dimensional Einstein manifold $(M^4, g)$.

