\section{Conclusion and Outlook}
\label{sec:conclusion}
% =========================================================================

Simplicial Quantum Gravity on $\Delta_4 \times \Delta_2$ demonstrates that the long-standing tensions between General Relativity and Quantum Field Theory stem not from physical pathology, but from the unwarranted assumption of smooth $C^\infty$ manifolds at sub-Planckian scales.

By replacing continuum infinities with regular simplices, $L^2$ actions with $L^\infty$-minimax variational bounds, and wave-packet reduction with Luis Caffarelli's free-boundary contact mechanics, the physical universe is revealed as an extraordinarily economical, singularity-free, and mathematically coherent geometric architecture.

